# Normalize line endings to LF for text files; the repo is LF-only and the
# pre-commit hook + CI enforce it.
* text=auto eol=lf
poetry.lock text eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary

# Fuzzing corpora are byte-exact test vectors, not text. The HTTP seeds make
# this load-bearing: CRLF framing is precisely what they exercise, and the
# `* text=auto eol=lf` rule above would rewrite every "\r\n" to "\n" on commit.
# The parser answers NeedMore rather than Ok for a bare-LF head, so normalized
# seeds would still "replay" green while testing something else entirely --
# a corpus quietly measuring the wrong thing is worse than no corpus.
cpp/fuzz/corpus-*/** -text
cpp/fuzz/corpus-regression-*/** -text
cpp/fuzz/make-seeds*.sh -text
